Kinora: IDCTs laid out for Emu68 (docs/architecture.md, section 14.2)

FFmpeg's 8-bit simple IDCT and its Xvid IDCT, bit for bit, in libavcodec/m68k/: a column
pass per mask of rows that hold coefficients (in 68k assembly for the simple IDCT), whole rows
for blocks with only column 0, one muls.w a product, clamping by table, and Xvid's clamped
stores fused into its column pass. ff_idctdsp_init() calls ff_idctdsp_init_m68k() when the
compiler targets m68k, which replaces the two only where FFmpeg chose them; lowres, other
depths and other IDCTs keep FFmpeg's. configure drops the arch with --disable-asm (which
libnix needs: it has no aligned allocations), so Kinora's build runs make with ARCH=m68k to
take libavcodec/m68k/Makefile in.

